  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 425 F. Line a rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "Combine the rice and water in a medium pot with a lid. Bring to a boil, cover, and reduce the heat to low. Cook 15 minutes until the water is absorbed.",
    "Whisk the miso, honey, rice vinegar, soy sauce, and ginger in a small bowl until smooth.",
    "Toss the green beans with the oil and salt. Spread them along one side of the baking sheet.",
    "Place the salmon on the other side of the pan. Spread the glaze over the top of each fillet.",
    "Bake 12 to 15 minutes. The salmon is done when it reaches 145 F and flakes easily, and the beans are tender with browned spots.",
    "Fluff the rice with a fork. Divide the rice among four plates and top with salmon and green beans.",
    "Spoon any glaze from the pan over the fish and sprinkle with the scallions."
